// Package ci.v1 is the gRPC API of ci-svc, the CI service of git2.
//
// ci-svc reads .git2-ci.yml, turns a push into a pipeline of jobs, queues
// the jobs for runners and keeps their status and logs. It serves two
// ports:
//   - The internal port: PipelineService, RunnerAdminService and
//     SecretService. Only other git2 services (dash-api, admin-api, the
//     event relay) reach it.
//   - The runner port: RunnerService only. Build hosts reach it, and every
//     call except RegisterRunner carries a runner token.
//
// Conventions for the whole package:
//   - IDs are UUIDs in canonical text form ("3f2b8c1e-..."). A malformed ID
//     is INVALID_ARGUMENT, not NOT_FOUND.
//   - Repository and user IDs are the ones issued by git-svc and auth-svc.
//     ci-svc stores IDs only, never names.
//   - On the internal port ci-svc does not authenticate or authorize
//     callers. The caller (dash-api, admin-api) checks the user's
//     permissions before calling.
//   - Errors use standard gRPC codes: INVALID_ARGUMENT, NOT_FOUND,
//     ALREADY_EXISTS, FAILED_PRECONDITION, UNAUTHENTICATED (runner port
//     only), RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED, UNAVAILABLE (retry later) and INTERNAL.
//     INTERNAL errors never contain SQL, paths or other internal details.
//   - List RPCs paginate per Google AIP-158.
//   - Domain events (PipelineFinished, ...) are defined in events.proto.
//
// Planned, not available yet:
//   - RetryJob (W4-W5).
//   - Artifacts: ListArtifacts, DownloadArtifact and the runner's
//     UploadArtifact (W6-W7).
//   - Secrets scoped to an owner (user or organization).

